{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Getting-Started","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"Getting started","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Migration-Guide","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Open-Publication","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/NavigatorOverview","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Content","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Search","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/TTS","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Accessibility","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Readium-LCP"],"anchor":"Guides","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Readium Swift toolkit enables you to develop reading apps for iOS and iPadOS. It provides built-in support for multiple publication formats such as EPUB, PDF, audiobooks, and comics."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[!NOTE]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Readium offers only low-level tools. You are responsible for creating a user interface for reading and managing books, as well as a data layer to store the user’s publications. The Test App is an example of such integration."}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"text":"Design principles","anchor":"Design-principles","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The toolkit has been designed following these core tenets:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Modular"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": It is divided into separate modules that can be used independently.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Extensible","type":"text"}]},{"text":": Integrators should be able to support a custom DRM, publication format or inject their own stylesheets without modifying the toolkit itself.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opiniated","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": We adhere to open standards but sometimes interpret them for practicality."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Packages","anchor":"Packages","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"text":"Main packages","anchor":"Main-packages","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ReadiumShared","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" contains shared ","type":"text"},{"code":"Publication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" models and utilities.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ReadiumStreamer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parses publication files (e.g. an EPUB) into a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Publication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" object.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"Navigator\/Navigator.md"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Specialized packages","anchor":"Specialized-packages","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReadiumOPDS"},{"text":" parses ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/opds.io"},{"text":" (both OPDS 1 and 2).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"Readium%20LCP.md"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Overview of the shared models (`ReadiumShared`)","anchor":"Overview-of-the-shared-models-ReadiumShared","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Readium toolkit provides models used as exchange types between packages.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Publication models","anchor":"Publication-models","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"text":"Publication","anchor":"Publication","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Publication","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and its sub-components represent a single publication – ebook, audiobook or comic. It is loosely based on the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/readium.org\/webpub-manifest\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"Publication","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"holds the metadata of a publication, such as its author or table of contents,"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"allows to read the contents of a publication, e.g. XHTML or audio resources,"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"provides additional services, for example content extraction or text search."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Link","anchor":"Link","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/readium.org\/webpub-manifest\/#24-the-link-object","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" holds a pointer (URL) to a resource or service along with additional metadata, such as its media type or title."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Publication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" contains several ","type":"text"},{"code":"Link","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" collections, for example:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"readingOrder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists the publication resources arranged in the order they should be read.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"resources","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" contains secondary resources necessary for rendering the ","type":"text"},{"code":"readingOrder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", such as an image or a font file.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tableOfContents"},{"type":"text","text":" represents the table of contents as a tree of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Link"},{"type":"text","text":" objects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"links"},{"type":"text","text":" exposes additional resources, such as a canonical link to the manifest or a search web service."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Locator","anchor":"Locator","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/readium.org\/architecture\/models\/locators\/"},{"type":"text","text":" represents a precise location in a publication resource in a format that can be stored and shared across reading systems. It is more accurate than a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Link"},{"type":"text","text":" and contains additional information about the location, e.g. progression percentage, position or textual context."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locator"},{"type":"text","text":" objects are used for various features, including:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"reporting the current progression in the publication","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"saving bookmarks, highlights and annotations"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"navigating search results"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Data models","anchor":"Data-models","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"text":"Asset","anchor":"Asset","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"Asset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represents a single file or package and provides access to its content. There are two types of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Asset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ContainerAsset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for packages which contains several resources, such as a ZIP archive."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ResourceAsset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for accessing a single resource, such as a JSON or PDF file.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Asset"},{"type":"text","text":" instances are obtained through an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AssetRetriever"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use the "},{"code":"asset.format","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to identify the media type and capabilities of the asset."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["if asset.format.conformsTo(.lcp) {","    \/\/ The asset is protected with LCP.","}","if asset.format.conformsTo(.epub) {","    \/\/ The asset represents an EPUB publication.","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Resource","anchor":"Resource","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resource"},{"type":"text","text":" provides read access to a single resource, such as a file or an entry in an archive."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Resource","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances are usually created by a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ResourceFactory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The toolkit ships with various implementations supporting different data access protocols such as local files or HTTP.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Container","anchor":"Container","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Container","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides read access to a collection of resources. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Container","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances representing an archive are usually created by an ","type":"text"},{"code":"ArchiveOpener","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The toolkit ships with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ZIPArchiveOpener","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" supporting both local and remote (HTTP) ZIP files.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Publication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects internally use a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Container","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to expose its content.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Opening a publication (`ReadiumStreamer`)","anchor":"Opening-a-publication-ReadiumStreamer","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To retrieve a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Publication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" object from a publication file like an EPUB or audiobook, you can use an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AssetRetriever","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"PublicationOpener","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Instantiate the required components.","let httpClient = DefaultHTTPClient()","let assetRetriever = AssetRetriever(","    httpClient: httpClient",")","let publicationOpener = PublicationOpener(","    parser: DefaultPublicationParser(","        httpClient: httpClient,","        assetRetriever: assetRetriever,","        pdfFactory: DefaultPDFDocumentFactory()","    )",")","","let url: URL = URL(...)","","\/\/ Retrieve an `Asset` to access the file content.","switch await assetRetriever.retrieve(url: url.anyURL.absoluteURL!) {","case .success(let asset):","    \/\/ Open a `Publication` from the `Asset`.","    switch await publicationOpener.open(asset: asset, allowUserInteraction: true, sender: view) {","    case .success(let publication):","        print(\"Opened \\(publication.metadata.title)\")","","    case .failure(let error):","        \/\/ Failed to access or parse the publication","    }","","case .failure(let error):","    \/\/ Failed to retrieve the asset","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"allowUserInteraction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter is useful when supporting a DRM like Readium LCP. It indicates if the toolkit can prompt the user for credentials when the publication is protected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"Open%20Publication.md","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Accessing the metadata of a publication","anchor":"Accessing-the-metadata-of-a-publication","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After opening a publication, you may want to read its metadata to insert a new entity into your bookshelf database, for instance. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"publication.metadata"},{"type":"text","text":" object contains everything you need, including "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authors"},{"type":"text","text":" and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"published"},{"type":"text","text":" date."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can retrieve the publication cover using ","type":"text"},{"code":"await publication.cover()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Rendering the publication on the screen (`ReadiumNavigator`)","anchor":"Rendering-the-publication-on-the-screen-ReadiumNavigator","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use a Readium navigator to present the publication to the user. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Navigator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" renders resources on the screen and offers APIs and user interactions for navigating the contents.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Please refer to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"Navigator\/Navigator.md","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Navigator guide"}],"overridingTitle":"Navigator guide"},{"text":" for more information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Search":{"kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Search","abstract":[{"text":"The Search API lets you look for a textual query in the content of a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Publication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". EPUB and PDF publications are supported.","type":"text"}],"title":"Searching a publication","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/search","type":"topic"},"https://readium.org/webpub-manifest/":{"url":"https:\/\/readium.org\/webpub-manifest\/","title":"Readium Web Publication Manifest","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Readium Web Publication Manifest"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/readium.org\/webpub-manifest\/"},"https://readium.org/webpub-manifest/#24-the-link-object":{"title":"Link object","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Link"},{"type":"text","text":" object"}],"url":"https:\/\/readium.org\/webpub-manifest\/#24-the-link-object","identifier":"https:\/\/readium.org\/webpub-manifest\/#24-the-link-object"},"Navigator/Navigator.md":{"url":"Navigator\/Navigator.md","title":"ReadiumNavigator renders the content of a publication","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReadiumNavigator"},{"type":"text","text":" renders the content of a publication"}],"identifier":"Navigator\/Navigator.md"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Content":{"title":"Extracting the content of a publication","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Content","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/content","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"article"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Accessibility":{"abstract":[{"text":"Some publications declare their accessibility features and limitations as metadata which broadly mirror the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/epub-a11y-11","type":"reference"},{"text":" specification.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Accessibility","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/accessibility","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Accessibility"},"Readium%20LCP.md":{"title":"ReadiumLCP downloads and decrypts LCP-protected publications","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReadiumLCP"},{"type":"text","text":" downloads and decrypts LCP-protected publications"}],"url":"Readium%20LCP.md","identifier":"Readium%20LCP.md"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Readium-LCP":{"title":"Supporting Readium LCP","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/readium-lcp","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Readium-LCP","abstract":[{"text":"You can use the Readium Swift toolkit to download and read publications that are protected with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.edrlab.org\/readium-lcp\/"},{"text":" DRM.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/NavigatorOverview":{"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/navigatoroverview","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/NavigatorOverview","title":"Navigator Overview","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn about the architecture, configuration, and usage of the Readium Navigator."}]},"https://www.edrlab.org/readium-lcp/":{"url":"https:\/\/www.edrlab.org\/readium-lcp\/","title":"Readium LCP","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Readium LCP"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/www.edrlab.org\/readium-lcp\/"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Migration-Guide":{"abstract":[{"text":"All migration steps necessary in reading apps to upgrade to major versions of the Swift Readium toolkit will be documented in this file.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/migration-guide","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Migration Guide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Migration-Guide","type":"topic"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Readium Swift Toolkit is a toolkit for ebooks, audiobooks, and comics written in Swift & Kotlin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium","url":"\/documentation\/readium","kind":"article","title":"Readium"},"https://readium.org/architecture/models/locators/":{"title":"Locator object","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locator"},{"type":"text","text":" object"}],"url":"https:\/\/readium.org\/architecture\/models\/locators\/","identifier":"https:\/\/readium.org\/architecture\/models\/locators\/"},"https://www.w3.org/TR/epub-a11y-11":{"url":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/epub-a11y-11","title":"EPUB Accessibility","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"EPUB Accessibility"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/epub-a11y-11"},"Open%20Publication.md":{"title":"See the dedicated user guide for more information","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See the dedicated user guide for more information"}],"url":"Open%20Publication.md","identifier":"Open%20Publication.md"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Open-Publication":{"type":"topic","title":"Opening a publication","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"To open a publication with Readium, you need to instantiate a couple of components: an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AssetRetriever"},{"type":"text","text":" and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PublicationOpener"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Open-Publication","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/open-publication","kind":"article"},"https://opds.io":{"url":"https:\/\/opds.io","title":"OPDS catalog feeds","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OPDS catalog feeds"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/opds.io"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/TTS":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/TTS","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/tts","title":"Text-to-speech","role":"article"}}}